---
/** Crawlable homepage explainer — same pattern as section8calculator.com. */
---

<section
  class="mt-16 rounded-2xl border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-surface-elevated)] px-6 py-8 sm:px-8"
  id="how-it-works"
  aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading"
>
  <h2 id="how-it-works-heading" class="font-display text-2xl text-[var(--color-ink)] sm:text-3xl">
    How this per diem calculator works
  </h2>
  <ol class="mt-6 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-base leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
    <li>
      <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Destination</strong> (state, city, or ZIP) maps to a GSA
      CONUS locality—or the standard CONUS rate if the town is not listed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Lodging</strong> uses the monthly GSA cap for each night
      of your trip (seasonal hotel ceilings, before tax).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">M&amp;IE</strong> is a daily meals and incidentals amount.
      First and last travel days are paid at 75% (FTR default).
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">FY2026 standard CONUS</strong> is $110 lodging + $68 M&amp;IE
      ($178 per full day) when no higher-cost locality applies.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong class="text-[var(--color-ink)]">Trip total</strong> = lodging nights + full-day M&amp;IE +
      75% first/last-day M&amp;IE, minus any government-provided meals you mark.
    </li>
  </ol>
  <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-[var(--color-ink-muted)]">
    Need the M&amp;IE breakdown table and FAQs?
    <a class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline" href="/calculator/gsa/">Open the full GSA calculator page</a>
    or <a class="font-semibold text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline" href="/methodology/">read the methodology</a>.
  </p>
</section>
